what is the terminal command to locate an ollama model on a serve
... r
 To locate an Ollama model on a server using the command line, 
you can use the `find` command in combination with the `grep` 
command. The `find` command searches for files that match a 
specified pattern, and the `grep` command searches for text 
strings within files. Here is an example command that will 
search for all files on the server that contain the string 
"OllamaModel" in their names:
```css
find / -name "*OllamaModel*" | grep -l ollama_model.py
```
In this command, `/` represents the root directory of the 
server, and `-name` is used to search for files with a specific  name pattern. The `*` wildcard matches any number of characters 
between the two occurrences of `OllamaModel`, so it will match 
files with names like "model\_OllamaModel.py" or 
"ollama\_model.py". The `grep -l` command then searches for 
lines containing the string "OllamaModel" and returns a list of 
files that contain it.

Note that this is just an example, and you may need to modify 
the command to fit your specific needs depending on the 
location and name of the file you are looking for. 

